# Release process (TimeLapser)

When making a **new release**, follow this workflow in order. **Do not skip steps.** Release only when the automated recording test passes.

## 1. Build and automated test (mandatory before any release)

- **Build the production app**  
  From project root:
  ```bash
  node scripts/build-electron-esbuild.js
  npx vite build
  ```
  (Or use `npm run dist:win` if you need the full Windows installer build.)
- **Run the automated recording test**  
  ```bash
  npm run test:recording
  ```
  This spawns Electron with the built app, runs the full recording test (monitors, regions, exports), and exits 0 only on success.
- **If the test fails or times out**  
  Fix the issue, rebuild, and run the test again. **Do not** create a release or push a tag until the test passes.
- **If the test passes**  
  Proceed to the pre-release checklist and release steps below.

## 2. Pre-release checklist

- **Version bump (mandatory when making packages)**  
  Bump the version in `package.json` (e.g. `1.0.7` → `1.0.8`). Use a patch bump for small fixes; minor/major when appropriate. Do not produce two packages with the same version.
- Update **README.md** if any user-facing features or behaviour changed.
- **Release notes (mandatory for every GitHub release)**  
  Create **both**:
  - `release-notes/vX.Y.Z.md` – used by the workflow as the release body.
  - `RELEASE_NOTES_vX.Y.Z.md` – same content in repo root for `gh release edit` and reference.
  Never push a tag without creating and committing these files first. See format below.

## 3. Release notes format (professional)

The release notes file is the **GitHub release description**. Keep it concise and scannable.

**Required structure:**

- **Title**: `# TimeLapser vX.Y.Z` (or `# Release notes – vX.Y.Z`).
- **Sections** with `##` headings, e.g. **New**, **Changed**, **Fixed**.
- **Bullets**: Use `-` with **bold** for the main idea, then a short explanation. One line per bullet when possible.
- **No** raw commit logs or vague “various fixes” without a one-line description.

End with an **Install** line:  
`Download the Windows installer from the [Releases](https://github.com/ImagineTheGames/TimeLapser/releases) page.`

### NEVER use generic-only release notes

- **Forbidden**: A release note that only has a generic heading (e.g. "Maintenance and stability", "Bug fixes", "Various improvements") with **no** concrete bullets under **New**, **Changed**, or **Fixed**.
- **Required**: Every release must list **actual changes** as bullets. If you don't know what changed, **derive them** before writing the note:
  - Inspect `git diff` or recent commits since the last tag.
  - Look at modified areas: `electron/`, `src/components/`, `package.json`, etc.
  - Write at least one bullet per meaningful user- or behaviour-facing change (e.g. "**Export dialog** – …", "**Settings** – …", "**Recording** – …").
- **Exception**: If the release is truly tooling-only (no user-facing or behaviour change), say so in one concrete line, e.g. "**Build** – Dependency or tooling updates only; no user-facing changes." Do **not** use a vague "Maintenance and stability" with nothing else.
- **When creating a release**: Never invent placeholder or filler text. If you have not yet determined what changed, **stop and gather the changes first** (diffs, commit messages), then write the notes.

## 4. Git and tag

- Commit all release-related changes (version, README, **both** `release-notes/vX.Y.Z.md` and `RELEASE_NOTES_vX.Y.Z.md`) with a clear message, e.g. `v1.0.8: add X, fix Y`.
- Push to `origin main`.
- **Only then** create and push the tag:  
  `git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "vX.Y.Z: short summary"` and `git push origin vX.Y.Z`.
- **Never** push a tag without release notes already committed and pushed.

## 5. GitHub release description (mandatory)

The GitHub release must **not** be left with only auto-generated changelog.

- After the workflow creates the release (on tag push), set the description from the notes file:
  ```bash
  gh release edit vX.Y.Z --notes-file RELEASE_NOTES_vX.Y.Z.md
  ```
- Confirm on the release page that the description shows the written patch notes.

## 6. Summary

- **Always** build and run `npm run test:recording` before a release. **Release only if the test passes.**
- Create **both** `release-notes/vX.Y.Z.md` and `RELEASE_NOTES_vX.Y.Z.md` (same content).
- **Never** push a tag without release notes. **Never** leave a GitHub release with only auto-generated or empty description.
- If the workflow did not attach the notes, run `gh release edit vX.Y.Z --notes-file RELEASE_NOTES_vX.Y.Z.md`.
